            "$2550$"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "answer": "First term $a_1 = 4(1) - 1 = 3$. Last term $a_{25} = 4(25) - 1 = 99$. Number of terms $n = 25$. $S_{25} = \\frac{25}{2}(3 + 99) = \\frac{25}{2}(102) = 25(51) = 1275$."
        },
        {
          "q": "How many terms are in the finite arithmetic sequence $7, 11, 15, \\dots, 87$?",
          "choices": [
            "$21$",
            "$20$",
